Falsifies `inter_process_communication::verification::a_bound_rendezvous_never_yields_a_sender`.

The defect: `bind_to_interrupt` sets the flag and leaves the sender queue alone. That is the
natural reading of milestone 603 (an interrupt's endpoint refuses every send), since `send`
already checks the flag, and it misses the senders that queued before the bind.

Expected to fail: `refused == usize::from(sender_was_queued)` when `seed` queued a sender, and
the closing `!matches!(e.receive(me), Receive::FromSender(..))`, because the driver's receive
collects the parked sender and wakes holding its words.

